From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 21:36:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 39/41] tee: qseecom: say why this driver exists alongside QTEE

Both the Kconfig help and the documentation framed QSEECOM as the interface for
platforms too old for smcinvoke, which invites the question of why the driver is
needed at all now that QTEE is upstream.

The actual reason is that the two interfaces are not alternative routes to the
same applications. An application is built against one of them, and a SoC can
offer both, so QTEE being available says nothing about whether the applications
in a platform's firmware can be reached through it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
